claim.claim-text:
a sheath member (8) comprising a tubular structure (34), wherein the tubular structure (34) comprises an elastic outer tubular layer (40) and an inner tubular layer (42);
wherein an inner surface of the elastic outer tubular layer (40) is adhered to an outer surface of the inner tubular layer (42) at a distal portion of the tubular wall structure (34); and
wherein the tubular structure (34) is movable between a folded configuration in which the elastic outer tubular layer (40) and the inner tubular layer (42) are folded at the distal portion of the tubular structure (34) and an unfolded configuration in which the elastic outer tubular layer (40) and the inner tubular layer (42) are expanded at the distal portion of the tubular structure (34).

urging the elastic outer tubular layer (40) and the inner tubular layer (42) from a folded configuration into a fully expanded, unfolded configuration;
reflowing a distal portion of the tubular structure (34) to adhere an outer surface of the inner tubular layer (42) to an inner surface of the outer tubular layer (40);
returning the reflowed distal portion of the tubular structure (34) to a folded configuration wherein the elastic outer tubular layer (40) and inner tubular layer (42) are folded at the distal portion;
compressing the reflowed distal portion under a heat shrink layer (74) to set the fold; and
removing the heat shrink layer (74).
